AI sandbox should have for regulated financial-services, risk, governance, or agentic use.

Guiding principles (draft):

Isolation by default and connectivity is treated as an exception.
Anything the model learns, accesses, creates or is permitted to do should not be allowed to become a production capability.
Production capabilities must be explicitly authorized, tested, bounded, and independently enforced outside the model.
Least privilege, least access and least autonomy.
Security and governance controls must be enforced by deterministic external systems.
Agents accountable for identities, not extensions of users. Agents actions should track back to users.
Scope is fixed, ambiguity should be resolved by humans.
All assumptions must be visible.
All agents including temporary creations as part of a process must have audit trail.
All data classification should be tracked throughout the lifecycle of operating in the model.
Behaviors should be fully tested and not just limited to output.
Untested = Untrusted.
Humans decide the irreversible, reversibility is a prerequisite.
End-to-end governance implementation not limited to checkpoints.
Full transparency of operations and controls.
Autonomy should be restricted, fully auditable lifecycle, physical isolation of sandbox, nothing leaves the sandbox independently - any operation conducted by AI leaving the sandbox should follow strict restrictions and be fully monitored.
